    {
      "id": "9_RoLNPjcBe4szezGj2Qk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 230.86393171228508,
      "y": 894.1284801348452,
      "width": 705.3346956896676,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 823568638,
      "version": 270,
      "versionNonce": 266568994,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792497504028,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Data Element: A data element is the smallest piece of information that\nwe want to send, i.e., bit 0 or 1.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Data Element: A data element is the smallest piece of information that we want to send, i.e., bit 0 or 1.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "y6bZZVVUagjJCf1T74ul2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 227.20586799398737,
      "y": 953.488368608487,
      "width": 487.5396728515625,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 264433122,
      "version": 100,
      "versionNonce": 263497570,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792497525615,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Signal Element: It is a shortest element of signal.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Signal Element: It is a shortest element of signal.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xvZHtJth3zW6Sj__8xDZW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 225.92906729073547,
      "y": 990.5117622393994,
      "width": 739.4099750566915,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1955911998,
      "version": 335,
      "versionNonce": 264161890,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792497532691,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Data Rate: Data elements are sent in one second. It is measured in\nbit/sec",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Data Rate: Data elements are sent in one second. It is measured in bit/sec",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3pckEfi_sEt-W4DwM9gRd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 226.99072078682866,
      "y": 1058.8106897916555,
      "width": 702.7074910776334,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1856954786,
      "version": 180,
      "versionNonce": 422311394,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792497608017,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Signal Rate/Baud rate: Signal elements are sent in one second. SI unit\nis baud.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Signal Rate/Baud rate: Signal elements are sent in one second. SI unit is baud.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "83VG4btPquOikGLfR5VuO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 227.54377313219385,
      "y": 1136.3001356897887,
      "width": 780.4420027812545,
      "height": 103.11211432078292,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1898826430,
      "version": 143,
      "versionNonce": 808042914,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792497833405,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Digital data conversion techniques encode binary information into signals\nsuitable for transmission over digital media like copper wires or optical fibers.\nDitigtal data to digital signal techniques are broadly classified into \"line\ncoding\" schemes",
      "fontSize": 20.622422864156583,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Digital data conversion techniques encode binary information into signals suitable for transmission over digital media like copper wires or optical fibers.\nDitigtal data to digital signal techniques are broadly classified into \"line coding\" schemes",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "GeR-cELHCZYnmOYAfpOzo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 248.34433654524923,
      "y": 1295.5704784858326,
      "width": 217.75982666015625,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1158572606,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 1962222526,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792497854322,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Unipolar Line Coding",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Unipolar Line Coding",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "DEGIYY6-cG_LqAqJzgtI9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 285.73780749478186,
      "y": 1333.4533249201306,
      "width": 713.5023186045257,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 775836862,
      "version": 140,
      "versionNonce": 1242511906,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792497874015,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "it represents binary ‘1’ with a positive voltage and ‘0’ with zero voltage.\nSimple systems like TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) circuits use it.\nits example is Unipolar NRZ.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "it represents binary ‘1’ with a positive voltage and ‘0’ with zero voltage. Simple systems like TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) circuits use it. its example is Unipolar NRZ.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wJg4k3LicBO5fIPeCQUGM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 280.3291183214693,
      "y": 1427.233155080946,
      "width": 718.4412822402486,
      "height": 80,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 52626110,
      "version": 138,
      "versionNonce": 1125062882,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792498052406,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The term “Uni” means “one,” indicating that only one type of voltage level—either positive\nor zero—is utilized. \nTypically, a positive voltage represents the data bit ‘1’, while 0V (ground) represents ‘0’.\nSince the system does not use negative voltages, it is referred to as unipolar.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The term “Uni” means “one,” indicating that only one type of voltage level—either positive or zero—is utilized. \nTypically, a positive voltage represents the data bit ‘1’, while 0V (ground) represents ‘0’. Since the system does not use negative voltages, it is referred to as unipolar.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "NEx3agLFBjSy7v90L6MQK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 314.48542593064576,
      "y": 1533.3825593133397,
      "width": 286.700439453125,
      "height": 20,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 470601534,
      "version": 52,
      "versionNonce": 1270633826,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792498087920,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Bit 1 → High Voltage (Positive Level)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Bit 1 → High Voltage (Positive Level)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-TGM2Zd2NxVlMn2dr3LND",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 387.84641716132955,
      "y": 1565.3733193711023,
      "width": 338.463623046875,
      "height": 20,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
