      "text": "Polar RZ (Return-to-Zero) Encoding",
      "fontSize": 17.936473589640816,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Polar RZ (Return-to-Zero) Encoding",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "tkCXGLtQT3Z3Xq0FmL4Iv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 319.4319043660832,
      "y": 2668.7043272870865,
      "width": 664.0952884528888,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aj",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 945777854,
      "version": 119,
      "versionNonce": 860459838,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792498508046,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In Polar RZ (Return-to-Zero) encoding, the same two voltage levels (positive and\nnegative) are utilized as in Polar NRZ-L, but with an important difference: the signal\nreturns to zero within each bit period.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In Polar RZ (Return-to-Zero) encoding, the same two voltage levels (positive and negative) are utilized as in Polar NRZ-L, but with an important difference: the signal returns to zero within each bit period.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yD5f57WPh9eirGGV383aC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 305.56142943792366,
      "y": 2753.1946680710475,
      "width": 686.6495042234307,
      "height": 40,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ak",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 306852862,
      "version": 196,
      "versionNonce": 1213129470,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792498560572,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Bit 1 → Starts at a High Voltage (Positive Level, e.g., +V) and returns to zero within\nthe bit period.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Bit 1 → Starts at a High Voltage (Positive Level, e.g., +V) and returns to zero within the bit period.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Df38jd_nuqUtbwtLqxqyG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 305.4503972257564,
      "y": 2819.7087689959244,
      "width": 688.2547716066229,
      "height": 40,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "al",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 899781346,
      "version": 170,
      "versionNonce": 1717717538,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792498570762,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Bit 0 → Starts at a Low Voltage (Negative Level, e.g., -V) and returns to zero within\nthe bit period.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Bit 0 → Starts at a Low Voltage (Negative Level, e.g., -V) and returns to zero within the bit period.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "mIsmWWUYuSnQnMvt31FSw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 295.0160319164136,
      "y": 2894.941702792887,
      "width": 398.255615234375,
      "height": 20,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "am",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 613857662,
      "version": 94,
      "versionNonce": 1475356990,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792498583731,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let’s assume the binary data to be transmitted is:",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let’s assume the binary data to be transmitted is:",
